/*!
  \page example_cxx_pcl_page Surface curvature in the Point Cloud Library (PCL)

  \section pcl_intro_sec Introduction

  This example uses %Ponca to compute the surface curvature of a point cloud with the
  <a href="https://pointclouds.org/" target="_blank">Point Cloud Library (PCL)</a>. It provides a PCL feature class,
  which could be incorporated in the "features" section of PCL, and a program that uses this feature and visualizes
  the result with a colormap.

  \subsection pcl_usage_sec Usage

  The example requires PCL (version 1.6 or later; it is skipped when PCL is not found by CMake):
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_pclwrapper
  \endcode

  \note With Visual Studio, if you have a problem with boost or PCL exceptions, enable C++ exceptions in Project ->
  Properties -> C/C++ -> Code Generation -> Enable C++ exceptions, and set it to "Yes (/EHsc)".

  The program displays two colored point clouds: on the left, the signed curvature estimated with %Ponca (GLS); on the
  right, the unsigned curvature estimated by PCL.
  \image html examples/pcl_wrapper.png "Surface curvature of a point cloud computed with the GLS method"

  \section pcl_wrapper_sec PCL wrapper

  \subsection pcl_wrapper_sec_pcl_wrapper_sec_h Declaration
  - `GlsPoint` defines how the point samples are represented,
  - `pcl::GlsCurvature` is the wrapper that brings the %Ponca algorithms into the PCL API.

  Source file: `pcl_wrapper.h`
  \include pcl/pcl_wrapper.h

  \subsection pcl_wrapper_sec_pcl_wrapper_sec_hpp Implementation
  Source file: `pcl_wrapper.hpp`
  \include pcl/pcl_wrapper.hpp

  \subsection pcl_wrapper_sec_pcl_wrapper_sec_cpp Instantiation
  Source file: `pcl_wrapper.cpp`
  \include pcl/pcl_wrapper.cpp

  \subsection pcl_main_sec Main program

  A program using the previous class, and visualizing the result.
  \include pcl/main.cpp
 */
